package Physics.Tests

use Libraries.Game.Collision.LocalCollisionPoints3D
use Libraries.Game.Collision.Shapes.Triangle

/*
A triangle smaller than the box's bottom face. The face is cut down to
the triangle, grown by its margin, so the contacts are at the grown
triangle's three corners.

Unless a test says otherwise, the triangle is a large one lying flat
at height 0, from MakeLargeTriangle, with the usual margin of 0.04, so
its thickened surface is at 0.04. The box is 0.5 on each side for
collisions (see RunBox), with no rotation, and the triangle is item A.
A box whose center is at 0.28 has its bottom at 0.03, so it sinks 0.01
into the surface.
*/
class BoxTriangleSmallTriangleTest is PhysicsTest
    on create
        SetName("Box and triangle: triangle smaller than the face")
    end

    action Run
        Triangle triangle
        triangle:Set(MakeVector(-0.1, 0, 0.1), MakeVector(0.1, 0, 0.1), MakeVector(0, 0, -0.1))
        triangle:SetMargin(0.04)
        LocalCollisionPoints3D points = RunBox(triangle, MakeTransform(0, 0.28, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0), false)
        CheckWhole("box small triangle: three contacts", points:GetPointCount(), 3)
        CheckAllContacts("box small triangle", points, 0, -1, 0, -0.01)
    end
end
